Using Amazon Web Services, set up and configure a basic web server using Amazon
EC2.
You are required to launch a virtual machine, install and run a web server, configure
network access, and modify instance resources to meet application requirements.
Steps to Execute:
1. Launch an Amazon EC2 instance using a suitable AMI (e.g., Amazon
Linux/Ubuntu).
2. Connect to the instance and install the Apache Web Server.
3. Start and enable the Apache service.
4. Modify the instance’s security group to allow HTTP (port 80) access.
5. Verify the web server by accessing it through the instance’s public IP
address.
6. Resize the instance by:
• Changing the instance type
• Modifying the EBS storage volume


